Package: qpmR
Title: Quarterly Projection Models for Monetary Policy Analysis
Version: 0.2.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person("Mustapha", "Mohammed", email = "muswaseja@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Build, solve, and simulate the semi-structural quarterly
    projection models (QPM) used in central-bank forecasting and policy
    analysis systems (FPAS). Provides a native R language for declaring
    gap-form models with model-consistent expectations, automatic handling
    of long lags and leads via auxiliary states, a generalized Schur (QZ)
    solver with Blanchard-Kahn diagnostics, steady-state computation,
    impulse responses, stochastic simulation, and unconditional forecasts
    with uncertainty bands. Ships the canonical small-open-economy model of
    Berg, Karam and Laxton (2006), IMF Working Paper 06/81, as a calibrated
    template.
